            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0473" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363/10–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-27T17:00:00+03:25">October 27, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 27—1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>787. Local press has been informed presumably by Iranian Government of receipt by
                    Prime Minister of my note regarding oil concession presented in accordance with
                    Department’s No. 622, dated October 16. As usual note was badly mangled by
                    Persian press and one purely imaginary statement attributed to my note stating
                    that “Iran is an independent country and therefore free to make its own
                    decisions and <pb facs="0474" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/> determine its own
                    destiny” has aroused curiosity of local Soviet Embassy which has requested copy
                    of actual note in question. I have informed Embassy that Persian version is
                    erroneous but that copy of actual note exchanged by my Government with Iran may
                    not be furnished it without consent of two Governments involved.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department, repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
